# Listed again, after the catch-all, because GitHub applies the last matching
# rule and because this path is the one that matters. standards/ci records that
# a required status check is matched by its name, so a pull request with write
# access can replace a caller with a stub emitting that name and exiting zero.
# The reusable cannot prevent it: the caller lives in the repository the pull
# request edits, and GitHub runs the pull request's version.
#
# The org accepts that risk while this is a single-maintainer repository, and
# the mitigation to apply the moment a human collaborator is added is
# ruleset-side: require review from Code Owners on this path, so a pull request
# neutralizing a caller cannot merge without the owner seeing the diff. That
# mitigation needs this file to already exist, which is why it is here now
# rather than on the day it is needed.
.github/workflows/      @Jaro-c
